   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( g \\) be the function defined by \\( g(x) = \\int_{1}^{x} \\left(t^{3} - 9 t\\right) \\, dt \\) for \\( -1 < x < 4 \\). Find the value of \\( x \\) at which \\( g \\) has a relative minimum."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 3
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "By the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus, \\( g'(x) = x^{3} - 9 x \\) for \\( -1 < x < 4 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            "x",
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               -3
            ],
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Set \\( g'(x) = 0 \\) and factor: \\( x(x + 3)(x - 3) = 0 \\), so \\( x = -3, 0, 3 \\).",
         "mathjson": 3
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Only \\( x = 0 \\) and \\( x = 3 \\) lie in \\( -1 < x < 4 \\); \\( x = -3 \\) is outside the interval on which \\( g \\) is defined, so it is not a critical point of \\( g \\).",
         "mathjson": 3
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "\\( g' \\) changes from negative to positive at \\( x = 3 \\) and from positive to negative at \\( x = 0 \\), so \\( g \\) has its relative minimum at \\( x = 3 \\).",
         "mathjson": 3
      }
   ],
